.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Pure mathematical transformation layer between 3D isometric world space (x, y, z) and 2D screen space (sx, sy)\&. 

In world coordinates:
.IP "\(bu" 2
+X points down-right along the isometric grid\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
+Y points down-left along the isometric grid\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
+Z points upward (elevation/height)\&. 
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static float sl::IsometricTransform::depth_sort_key (float x, float y, float z = \fC0\&.0f\fP)\fC [inline]\fP, \fC [static]\fP"

.PP
Calculate depth sorting key for back-to-front rendering order\&. (X + Y) must dominate the key so that a tile which is diagonally further forward always renders after (on top of) every tile diagonally behind it, no matter how tall either column is\&. Z is only used to order layers within the same (x, y) column, and must never be large enough to outweigh a one-unit change in X or Y (which would let a tall column behind erroneously paint over a shorter column in front, hiding its top face)\&. 
.SS "\fBIsoBounds\fP sl::IsometricTransform::visible_bounds (float left, float top, float right, float bottom, float min_z = \fC0\&.0f\fP, float max_z = \fC0\&.0f\fP) const\fC [inline]\fP"

.PP
Compute visible grid bounds for a 2D screen rectangle [left, top, right, bottom]\&. 
.PP
